1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,266
I'm Peppa Pig. [grunts]

2
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:07,600
-This is my little brother George.
-[grunts]

3
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:10,299
-This is Mommy Pig.
-[grunts]

4
00:00:10,366 --> 00:00:12,666
-And this is Daddy Pig.
-[grunts]

5
00:00:12,733 --> 00:00:14,200
[laughing]

6
00:00:14,266 --> 00:00:15,766
Peppa Pig. [grunts]

7
00:00:16,666 --> 00:00:19,000
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

8
00:00:19,066 --> 00:00:21,099
[narrator] Peppa, George, and Suzy Sheep

9
00:00:21,166 --> 00:00:24,066
have had a sleepover
at Rebecca Rabbit's house.

10
00:00:24,433 --> 00:00:29,066
It's fun having carrots for breakfast,
Mommy Rabbit.

11
00:00:29,133 --> 00:00:32,100
Yes, we always have carrots for breakfast.

12
00:00:32,166 --> 00:00:36,133
I could eat carrots all day,
but I'd better go to work.

13
00:00:36,199 --> 00:00:37,166
Have a nice day.

14
00:00:37,233 --> 00:00:38,466
[in unison] Bye-bye.

15
00:00:38,533 --> 00:00:41,400
Mommy Rabbit, why don't you work?

16
00:00:41,466 --> 00:00:45,733
I do work, Suzy. Who do you think
looks after these two little bunnies?

17
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:47,733
You do, Mommy. [giggles]

18
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:51,066
And you can help me
by tidying up your toys, please,

19
00:00:51,133 --> 00:00:53,066
before someone trips over them.

20
00:00:53,133 --> 00:00:54,000
[doorbell rings]

21
00:00:54,066 --> 00:00:55,533
That'll be my sister.

22
00:00:55,599 --> 00:00:56,466
Hello.

23
00:00:56,533 --> 00:00:59,533
-Hello, Miss Rabbit.
-Aunty.

24
00:00:59,599 --> 00:01:00,699
I can't stop long,

25
00:01:00,766 --> 00:01:05,066
I've got lots of work to do today.
I've got the supermarket checkout,

26
00:01:05,133 --> 00:01:07,633
the ice cream stall, and the bus to drive.

27
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:09,666
See you later then, sister.

28
00:01:09,733 --> 00:01:11,333
Bye, sister.

29
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,366
Whoops. Whoa!

30
00:01:13,433 --> 00:01:16,466
Miss Rabbit has tripped over one
of Richard's toys.

31
00:01:16,533 --> 00:01:18,300
Oh, my ankle.

32
00:01:18,366 --> 00:01:23,333
-I can still hop to work. Aah. Ooh.
-No, you stay here and get better.

33
00:01:23,399 --> 00:01:25,600
But I've got so much work to do.

34
00:01:25,666 --> 00:01:29,033
I'll do your work for you.
Which job is first?

35
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:30,399
The supermarket.

36
00:01:30,466 --> 00:01:31,366
Okay.

37
00:01:31,433 --> 00:01:33,466
Rebecca, look after your aunty.

38
00:01:33,533 --> 00:01:34,600
Yes, Mommy.

39
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:40,000
Mommy Rabbit has arrived
at the supermarket.

40
00:01:40,066 --> 00:01:42,433
Thank goodness you're here, Miss Rabbit.

41
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:45,399
Miss Rabbit is ill.
I'll be doing her job today.

42
00:01:45,466 --> 00:01:47,133
Are you not Miss Rabbit?

43
00:01:47,199 --> 00:01:51,399
No, I'm her sister, Mommy Rabbit.
Is this where I sit?

44
00:01:51,466 --> 00:01:55,466
Uh, yes. Have you ever worked
a checkout before?

45
00:01:55,533 --> 00:01:57,666
-No.
-How much is this?

46
00:01:57,733 --> 00:01:59,233
Oh, I don't know.

47
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:02,100
-I've got a voucher.
-Do you take book tokens?

48
00:02:02,166 --> 00:02:03,666
Can I pay with a card?

49
00:02:03,733 --> 00:02:05,100
Um...

50
00:02:05,566 --> 00:02:08,466
Suzy Sheep is dressed up
in her nurse's costume.

51
00:02:08,533 --> 00:02:12,133
Don't worry. I'm only a pretend nurse.

52
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:15,600
Stick your tongue out and say, "aah."

53
00:02:15,666 --> 00:02:17,100
Aah!

54
00:02:17,166 --> 00:02:18,666
[telephone rings]

55
00:02:19,066 --> 00:02:23,166
Rebecca Rabbit's house.
Who's speaking, please?

56
00:02:23,233 --> 00:02:26,700
-It's Mommy Rabbit. Is everything okay?
-[Peppa] Yes.

57
00:02:26,766 --> 00:02:29,666
Good, because this job
is gonna take me all day.

58
00:02:29,733 --> 00:02:33,066
What about Miss Rabbit's other jobs?

59
00:02:33,133 --> 00:02:34,600
We'll need more help.

60
00:02:35,733 --> 00:02:37,566
[telephone rings]

61
00:02:38,133 --> 00:02:39,166
Uh...

62
00:02:39,233 --> 00:02:41,100
Miss Rabbit's ice cream stall.

63
00:02:41,166 --> 00:02:44,433
Daddy. Why are you buying an ice cream?

64
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:50,400
Oh, Peppa. I was on the way to the gym
when I thought an ice cream would be nice.

65
00:02:50,466 --> 00:02:53,200
[grunts] Miss Rabbit is ill.

66
00:02:53,266 --> 00:02:56,299
You've got to sell the ice cream today.

67
00:02:56,366 --> 00:02:59,700
Oh ho! I'm an expert at ice cream.

68
00:02:59,766 --> 00:03:02,366
Can I have a cherry ice cream?

69
00:03:02,433 --> 00:03:07,400
Uh... Strawberry. Vanilla.
Chocolate. Banana.

70
00:03:07,466 --> 00:03:10,233
With pistachio and strawberry, please.

71
00:03:10,299 --> 00:03:12,100
Ah. Strawberry.

72
00:03:12,766 --> 00:03:15,033
Oh. It's melted.

73
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:18,466
How about ice cream soup instead?

74
00:03:21,266 --> 00:03:22,133
[line rings]

75
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:25,666
[woofs] Granddad Dog's breakdown service.

76
00:03:25,733 --> 00:03:31,166
[grunts] Miss Rabbit is ill.
Can you drive her bus today?

77
00:03:31,233 --> 00:03:32,700
Of course, Peppa.

78
00:03:32,766 --> 00:03:34,033
[horn honks]

79
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,733
[woofs] All aboard.

80
00:03:42,466 --> 00:03:45,133
Mommy Sheep's car has broken down.

81
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:48,000
[phone rings]

82
00:03:48,066 --> 00:03:51,100
[woofs] Granddad Dog's breakdown service.

83
00:03:51,366 --> 00:03:55,166
-[bleats] Can you rescue me, please?
-I'll be straight there.

84
00:03:55,733 --> 00:03:56,633
[chattering]

85
00:03:56,700 --> 00:03:59,200
We would like to apologize

86
00:03:59,266 --> 00:04:03,766
for any inconvenience
this may cause to your journey.

87
00:04:04,066 --> 00:04:06,466
Driving a bus is quite hard.

88
00:04:07,100 --> 00:04:09,433
Selling ice cream is quite hard.

89
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:12,600
Running a supermarket checkout
is quite hard.

90
00:04:14,033 --> 00:04:16,466
[laughing and noisemaking]

91
00:04:16,533 --> 00:04:17,399
Uh...

92
00:04:17,466 --> 00:04:20,266
I'm feeling better. Can I get up now?

93
00:04:20,333 --> 00:04:26,266
No, you must lie very still,
but, please, keep breathing.

94
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:27,500
[door closes]

95
00:04:28,099 --> 00:04:29,066
-[Daddy Pig grunts]
-[Granddad Dog woofs]

96
00:04:29,133 --> 00:04:33,566
-Are you feeling any better, Miss Rabbit?
-It's not easy doing all your jobs.

97
00:04:33,633 --> 00:04:36,200
It's not easy looking after
your little bunnies.

98
00:04:36,266 --> 00:04:37,133
[both laugh]

99
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:39,766
You will be back to work tomorrow,
won't you?

100
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,466
Yes, and you'll be back at home,
won't you?

101
00:04:42,533 --> 00:04:43,400
Yes.

102
00:04:43,466 --> 00:04:45,766
[laughing]

103
00:04:47,366 --> 00:04:49,666
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

104
00:04:50,666 --> 00:04:53,300
[narrator] Peppa has come
to play with Suzy Sheep.

105
00:04:53,366 --> 00:04:56,566
-[giggles] Hello, Suzy.
-Hello, Peppa.

106
00:04:56,633 --> 00:04:59,700
Why have you got that mask on your face?

107
00:04:59,766 --> 00:05:02,033
So people don't know it's me.

108
00:05:02,099 --> 00:05:04,733
I'm in a... [whispers] secret club.

109
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:07,633
Ooh. Can I be in your secret club?

110
00:05:07,700 --> 00:05:08,733
Shh.

111
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:14,200
It's not easy to get in to.
You have to say the secret word.

112
00:05:14,266 --> 00:05:15,800
What word?

113
00:05:16,033 --> 00:05:18,800
-Flob-a-dobble.
-Flob-a-dobble?

114
00:05:19,033 --> 00:05:20,333
Right, you're in.

115
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:21,599
[both giggle]

116
00:05:21,666 --> 00:05:23,133
[bicycle bell rings]

117
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:25,233
Danny Dog has come to play.

118
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:28,400
[barks] Hello, Peppa. Hello, Suzy.

119
00:05:28,466 --> 00:05:29,666
Shh.

120
00:05:29,733 --> 00:05:32,666
-What?
-I'm in a secret club.

121
00:05:32,733 --> 00:05:34,300
I'm in it, too.

122
00:05:34,366 --> 00:05:36,033
-Ooh.
-[bicycle bells ring]

123
00:05:36,099 --> 00:05:41,000
Pedro Pony, Candy Cat,
and Rebecca Rabbit have come to play.

124
00:05:41,066 --> 00:05:42,766
-Hello.
-Shh!

125
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,366
[barks] Suzy and Peppa
are in a secret club.

126
00:05:46,433 --> 00:05:49,133
Can we join your secret club?

127
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:52,200
It's very hard to get into.

128
00:05:52,266 --> 00:05:55,233
You have to say the secret word:

129
00:05:55,366 --> 00:05:57,133
Shallamakooky!

130
00:05:57,200 --> 00:05:59,433
[all] Shallamakooky?

131
00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:01,466
That's not the word I said.

132
00:06:01,533 --> 00:06:05,200
It changes all the time to keep it secret.

133
00:06:05,266 --> 00:06:08,133
-Oh.
-Are we in the secret club now?

134
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:09,500
You're in.

135
00:06:09,566 --> 00:06:11,233
What do we do?

136
00:06:11,300 --> 00:06:14,400
We do secret things in secret.

137
00:06:14,466 --> 00:06:18,733
And secretly go on secret missions.
[giggle]

138
00:06:18,799 --> 00:06:21,666
[sighs] I don't know
what you're talking about.

139
00:06:21,733 --> 00:06:24,299
Show us how you do a secret mission.

140
00:06:24,366 --> 00:06:26,333
[in unison] Yes. Show us.

141
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:28,233
Uh, Peppa can do it.

142
00:06:28,299 --> 00:06:31,033
You've got the mask on, Suzy.

143
00:06:31,099 --> 00:06:35,366
Okay.
My secret mission is to get biscuits.

144
00:06:35,433 --> 00:06:37,033
Watch this.

145
00:06:38,299 --> 00:06:41,200
Suzy Sheep is trying not to be seen.

146
00:06:45,566 --> 00:06:49,333
Mommy, can I have some biscuits
for my friends, please?

147
00:06:49,400 --> 00:06:51,299
Of course. Here you are.

148
00:06:51,366 --> 00:06:52,633
Thank you, Mommy.

149
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:59,066
Suzy Sheep has returned with the biscuits.

150
00:06:59,133 --> 00:07:00,299
[in unison] Hooray!

151
00:07:00,366 --> 00:07:01,366
Shh!

152
00:07:01,433 --> 00:07:02,433
[quietly] Hooray.

153
00:07:03,700 --> 00:07:06,200
-Did anyone see you?
-No.

154
00:07:06,266 --> 00:07:08,366
Well, only a grownup.

155
00:07:08,433 --> 00:07:09,599
Look out.

156
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:13,299
Would you like juice
to go with your biscuits?

157
00:07:13,366 --> 00:07:14,433
What biscuits?

158
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:17,099
The biscuits I just gave you
for your friends.

159
00:07:17,166 --> 00:07:19,299
Oh, Suzy.

160
00:07:19,366 --> 00:07:20,466
What's the matter?

161
00:07:20,533 --> 00:07:23,500
We're in a secret club,
doing secret things,

162
00:07:23,566 --> 00:07:26,400
and Suzy's told everyone.

163
00:07:26,466 --> 00:07:29,066
Oh, can I be in your secret club, please?

164
00:07:29,666 --> 00:07:33,200
Please? I've always wanted
to be in a secret club.

165
00:07:33,266 --> 00:07:35,666
It's very hard to get into.

166
00:07:35,733 --> 00:07:38,799
You must say the secret word.

167
00:07:39,033 --> 00:07:40,066
Which is?

168
00:07:40,133 --> 00:07:42,033
Pica-needle-noodle.

169
00:07:42,099 --> 00:07:43,766
Pica-needle-noodle?

170
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,500
That's it. You're in.

171
00:07:46,566 --> 00:07:48,233
What happens now?

172
00:07:48,299 --> 00:07:49,766
-Look out.
-[car horn honks]

173
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:51,433
It's Daddy Pig.

174
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:53,433
You talk to my daddy.

175
00:07:53,500 --> 00:07:57,266
But don't say anything
about our secret club.

176
00:07:58,233 --> 00:07:59,466
Hello?

177
00:07:59,533 --> 00:08:02,666
Ah. There you are, Mommy Sheep.
What's new?

178
00:08:03,066 --> 00:08:04,666
[stammers]

179
00:08:04,733 --> 00:08:06,033
Secret club.

180
00:08:06,099 --> 00:08:07,700
Oh, no.

181
00:08:07,766 --> 00:08:12,133
Ooh. I always wanted to be
in a secret club. Can I join, please?

182
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:16,233
You can't join, Daddy,
because you are grown up.

183
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:18,799
Uh, my mommy is grown up.

184
00:08:19,033 --> 00:08:23,200
Well, you have to know the magic word.

185
00:08:23,266 --> 00:08:24,533
Which is?

186
00:08:24,633 --> 00:08:26,733
Papa-deedle-doodle-dum.

187
00:08:26,799 --> 00:08:29,266
Papa-deedle-doodle-dum.

188
00:08:29,333 --> 00:08:30,666
[in unison] You're in.

189
00:08:30,733 --> 00:08:32,066
What do I do now?

190
00:08:32,133 --> 00:08:33,100
Look out.

191
00:08:33,699 --> 00:08:34,799
It's Mommy Pig.

192
00:08:35,033 --> 00:08:38,199
Follow Mommy in secret.

193
00:08:41,233 --> 00:08:42,366
[rustling]

194
00:08:42,433 --> 00:08:43,433
Daddy Pig?

195
00:08:43,500 --> 00:08:45,300
Ah. Hello, Mommy Pig.

196
00:08:45,366 --> 00:08:47,333
What are you doing in that bush?

197
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:50,100
Um, uh... Secret club.

198
00:08:50,533 --> 00:08:51,366
[all sigh]

199
00:08:51,433 --> 00:08:54,500
I've always wanted
to be in a secret club.

200
00:08:54,566 --> 00:08:57,666
We can't have everyone in the secret club.

201
00:08:57,733 --> 00:09:00,633
-It wouldn't be a secret.
-Oh.

202
00:09:00,699 --> 00:09:05,533
I suppose it doesn't have
to be a "secret" secret club.

203
00:09:05,600 --> 00:09:09,433
[grunts] It can be
The Everybody Secret Club.

204
00:09:09,500 --> 00:09:12,100
And everybody can be in it.

205
00:09:12,166 --> 00:09:13,199
Oh, goody.

206
00:09:13,300 --> 00:09:15,066
[all laughing]

207
00:09:18,733 --> 00:09:21,633
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

208
00:09:21,699 --> 00:09:23,666
[narrator] Peppa, George, and Granny Pig

209
00:09:23,733 --> 00:09:27,166
are going out for a day
on Grandpa Pig's boat.

210
00:09:27,233 --> 00:09:29,800
[grunts] Ahoy there, Peppa and George.

211
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:35,000
-We're ready to go sailing.
-I'll move the boat a bit nearer.

212
00:09:35,066 --> 00:09:38,199
Careful you don't hit that big stick,
Grandpa.

213
00:09:38,266 --> 00:09:42,066
That's a mooring post. I won't hit it.

214
00:09:43,466 --> 00:09:44,333
Oh.

215
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:48,199
Grandpa, there's a big hole in your boat.

216
00:09:48,266 --> 00:09:50,500
It's just a scratch.

217
00:09:51,666 --> 00:09:55,199
Ooh. Grandpa's boat is sinking.

218
00:09:55,266 --> 00:09:57,600
Quick, Grandpa Pig, jump off.

219
00:09:57,666 --> 00:10:01,533
A captain never leaves his sinking ship.

220
00:10:04,266 --> 00:10:07,699
Grandpa Pig's boat has sunk
to the bottom of the river.

221
00:10:09,300 --> 00:10:10,800
It is Granddad Dog.

222
00:10:11,166 --> 00:10:12,100
[woofs]

223
00:10:12,166 --> 00:10:15,400
Ahoy there, Grandpa Pig.
Lovely day for a sail.

224
00:10:15,466 --> 00:10:18,199
Um, yes. Ahoy there.

225
00:10:18,266 --> 00:10:22,600
I'm taking my boat to the boatyard today.
Going to get a few repairs done.

226
00:10:22,666 --> 00:10:27,533
Eh, would you mind taking my boat
to the boatyard, too, please?

227
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:28,733
Of course.

228
00:10:29,133 --> 00:10:31,199
Where is your boat?

229
00:10:31,266 --> 00:10:33,400
Um, I'm standing on it.

230
00:10:33,466 --> 00:10:35,666
[laughs] Has it sunk?

231
00:10:36,033 --> 00:10:37,800
Well, a little bit.

232
00:10:38,033 --> 00:10:41,366
I'm surprised your boat
didn't sink a long time ago.

233
00:10:41,433 --> 00:10:45,366
What? It's a better boat
than that rust bucket of yours.

234
00:10:45,433 --> 00:10:47,033
[barking and grunting]

235
00:10:47,100 --> 00:10:50,733
Granddad Dog and Grandpa Pig
are very best friends.

236
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:52,633
Catch this, captain.

237
00:10:52,699 --> 00:10:54,233
Aye, aye, skipper.

238
00:10:54,699 --> 00:10:56,366
[engine starts]

239
00:10:58,100 --> 00:11:02,600
Granddad Dog's truck has lifted
Grandpa Pig's boat out of the water.

240
00:11:03,133 --> 00:11:04,433
[Peppa and George] Wow.

241
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:06,500
Next stop, the boatyard.

242
00:11:08,033 --> 00:11:10,199
[Peppa] What's a boatyard?

243
00:11:10,266 --> 00:11:14,400
A boatyard, Peppa,
is where broken boats get mended.

244
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:19,166
This is Grampy Rabbit's boatyard.

245
00:11:20,066 --> 00:11:22,433
Ahoy there, me hearties.

246
00:11:22,500 --> 00:11:25,000
Ahoy there, Grampy Rabbit.

247
00:11:25,233 --> 00:11:29,033
Whoo. Who did that to your boat,
Grandpa Pig?

248
00:11:29,100 --> 00:11:32,433
Um, someone drove it into a mooring post.

249
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:34,233
It went crash.

250
00:11:34,300 --> 00:11:37,166
And made a big hole there.

251
00:11:37,233 --> 00:11:41,300
You should never let other people
steer your boat, Grandpa Pig.

252
00:11:41,366 --> 00:11:44,166
Uh... Yes. Can you mend it?

253
00:11:44,233 --> 00:11:47,366
Of course.
I just need to size up the damage.

254
00:11:47,433 --> 00:11:51,466
Grampy Rabbit is measuring the hole
in Grandpa Pig's boat.

255
00:11:51,533 --> 00:11:54,600
Now I need to find something
to patch it up.

256
00:11:55,199 --> 00:11:58,166
[grunts] It must be good
to know how to mend a boat.

257
00:11:58,233 --> 00:12:01,666
Oh. It takes years
to learn how to mend a boat.

258
00:12:01,733 --> 00:12:04,633
How long have you been mending boats?

259
00:12:04,699 --> 00:12:05,600
Years.

260
00:12:06,566 --> 00:12:10,600
Grampy Rabbit has collected
lots of scrap metal to mend boats with.

261
00:12:10,666 --> 00:12:13,566
Now, this is a gold mine.

262
00:12:13,633 --> 00:12:15,733
It's a pile of rubbish.

263
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:19,533
Ah, but you can make things
from piles of rubbish.

264
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:20,733
Like what?

265
00:12:20,800 --> 00:12:23,100
[Grampy Rabbit] Like submarines.

266
00:12:23,166 --> 00:12:24,233
[Peppa and George] Wow.

267
00:12:24,300 --> 00:12:27,400
Grampy Rabbit has made
a submarine out of rubbish.

268
00:12:27,466 --> 00:12:29,133
Does it actually work?

269
00:12:29,199 --> 00:12:30,699
Watch this.

270
00:12:32,033 --> 00:12:33,766
It fills up with water.

271
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,433
So, it's very good at going down.

272
00:12:36,633 --> 00:12:39,033
But not so good at coming back up.

273
00:12:39,533 --> 00:12:42,433
Now, this is what I've been looking for.

274
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:44,800
It's a washing machine.

275
00:12:45,033 --> 00:12:48,699
It's the fix for Grandpa Pig's boat,
is what it is.

276
00:12:50,133 --> 00:12:54,199
You're going to mend my boat
with a bit of washing machine?

277
00:12:54,266 --> 00:12:55,466
Yes.

278
00:12:59,599 --> 00:13:02,033
That's as good as new.

279
00:13:02,099 --> 00:13:03,533
Hooray!

280
00:13:03,599 --> 00:13:05,366
Now we test it.

281
00:13:06,333 --> 00:13:07,699
Prepare for launch.

282
00:13:07,766 --> 00:13:09,099
Aye, aye.

283
00:13:12,199 --> 00:13:14,166
Amazing. It floats.

284
00:13:14,233 --> 00:13:19,000
-You sound surprised.
-Yes, usually they sink on the first go.

285
00:13:19,066 --> 00:13:22,566
[grunts] Now we can go for our day
on the river.

286
00:13:22,633 --> 00:13:24,800
What a splendid idea.

287
00:13:25,033 --> 00:13:26,433
This is the life.

288
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:31,599
Out on a boat,
with just the sea and the sky.

289
00:13:31,666 --> 00:13:36,433
I know a song about the sea and the sky.
Do you want to hear it?

290
00:13:36,500 --> 00:13:37,733
No, thank you.

291
00:13:37,800 --> 00:13:39,266
Yes, please.

292
00:13:39,333 --> 00:13:41,300
♪ I got up this morning ♪

293
00:13:41,366 --> 00:13:44,099
♪ The sea was still there ♪

294
00:13:44,166 --> 00:13:46,333
♪ And so was the sky ♪

295
00:13:46,400 --> 00:13:47,766
[all laugh]

296
00:13:50,233 --> 00:13:53,133
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

297
00:13:53,633 --> 00:13:56,133
[narrator] Peppa and her friends
are at playgroup.

298
00:13:56,199 --> 00:13:57,533
Today, children,

299
00:13:57,599 --> 00:14:03,133
we are going to learn about instruments
that you shake, rattle, and bang.

300
00:14:03,199 --> 00:14:04,400
Hooray!

301
00:14:04,466 --> 00:14:08,300
First choose an instrument each
from the music room.

302
00:14:08,366 --> 00:14:10,666
[chattering and giggling]

303
00:14:12,099 --> 00:14:13,733
I've got drums.

304
00:14:13,800 --> 00:14:18,733
They are called bongo drums, Danny.
You bang them with your hands like this:

305
00:14:21,666 --> 00:14:25,233
[bleats] I've got a flat bongo drum.

306
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:28,366
That is a bodhran. It Is Irish.

307
00:14:28,433 --> 00:14:31,066
You beat it with a little stick,
like this:

308
00:14:32,266 --> 00:14:34,400
I've got a tambourine.

309
00:14:35,233 --> 00:14:39,566
Very good, Pedro.
You can also shake it like this:

310
00:14:40,533 --> 00:14:41,566
[all] Ooh.

311
00:14:43,199 --> 00:14:45,166
[grunts] I've got a big drum.

312
00:14:45,566 --> 00:14:48,099
Ah! The bass drum.

313
00:14:48,166 --> 00:14:52,366
[meows] I don't know what this is called,
but it's scrape-y.

314
00:14:53,566 --> 00:14:56,000
That, Candy, is called a guiro,

315
00:14:56,066 --> 00:14:59,233
and it comes all the way
from South America.

316
00:14:59,300 --> 00:15:00,199
[in unison] Wow.

317
00:15:00,266 --> 00:15:02,233
How did it get here?

318
00:15:02,300 --> 00:15:04,466
I brought it back from my holiday.

319
00:15:04,533 --> 00:15:06,099
What are these?

320
00:15:06,766 --> 00:15:08,500
They are maracas.

321
00:15:08,566 --> 00:15:12,199
I brought them back
from my holiday in Spain.

322
00:15:12,266 --> 00:15:14,800
-This is a triangle.
-[dings]

323
00:15:15,033 --> 00:15:19,199
My dad sells these in boxes of ten.

324
00:15:19,266 --> 00:15:21,800
Thank you, Freddy, I will remember that.

325
00:15:22,033 --> 00:15:24,800
You don't need to go on holiday
to get them.

326
00:15:25,033 --> 00:15:25,766
Thank you.

327
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:27,233
[trumpets]

328
00:15:27,300 --> 00:15:28,400
What are these?

329
00:15:28,466 --> 00:15:30,466
These are castanets.

330
00:15:30,533 --> 00:15:35,500
-My dad sells them in boxes of five.
-Thank you, Freddy.

331
00:15:35,666 --> 00:15:38,133
[clicking]

332
00:15:38,199 --> 00:15:39,133
Olé!

333
00:15:39,199 --> 00:15:42,433
That is how you play the castanets.

334
00:15:42,500 --> 00:15:44,000
Here you are, Emily.

335
00:15:44,066 --> 00:15:46,333
Do I have to do the dance?

336
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:50,033
[laughs] No. Just make
the clickety-clack noise.

337
00:15:50,099 --> 00:15:51,366
-[clicking]
-[giggles]

338
00:15:51,433 --> 00:15:54,733
Ah. I see Rebecca has cymbals.

339
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:56,133
[squeaks] Yes.

340
00:15:56,633 --> 00:15:57,500
[laughs]

341
00:15:57,566 --> 00:16:00,366
Now you know
what your instruments sound like,

342
00:16:00,433 --> 00:16:02,400
we can play them all together.

343
00:16:02,533 --> 00:16:04,566
-Ready...
-Steady, go.

344
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:08,633
Stop, stop, stop.

345
00:16:08,800 --> 00:16:12,199
That is not music. That is just noise.

346
00:16:12,266 --> 00:16:14,400
Anybody can bang, bang, bang.

347
00:16:14,466 --> 00:16:16,066
But to make music,

348
00:16:16,133 --> 00:16:19,766
you have to listen to each other,
and keep in time.

349
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:24,699
Madame Gazelle,
I can't listen and do music.

350
00:16:24,766 --> 00:16:25,766
Can you clap?

351
00:16:26,566 --> 00:16:27,566
Yes.

352
00:16:27,633 --> 00:16:30,633
If you can clap, you can make music.

353
00:16:31,633 --> 00:16:34,033
All the girls, please, copy me.

354
00:16:36,099 --> 00:16:37,500
Now boys.

355
00:16:40,599 --> 00:16:43,666
Madame Gazelle
has made the clapping into music.

356
00:16:43,733 --> 00:16:45,566
And stop.

357
00:16:45,633 --> 00:16:46,566
[all giggle]

358
00:16:46,633 --> 00:16:51,333
Now we will learn how
to play our instruments together.

359
00:16:52,766 --> 00:16:55,266
The parents have come
to pick up the children.

360
00:16:55,333 --> 00:16:57,333
Ah, you're just in time.

361
00:16:57,400 --> 00:17:01,800
May I present
The Shake, Rattle and Bang Orchestra.

362
00:17:02,033 --> 00:17:03,066
Hooray!

363
00:17:03,133 --> 00:17:06,433
Children, ready, steady, go.

364
00:17:14,666 --> 00:17:16,133
Bravo.

365
00:17:17,266 --> 00:17:21,599
Perhaps some of my old pupils
would like to join in, too.

366
00:17:21,666 --> 00:17:24,633
Find your instruments, children.

367
00:17:24,700 --> 00:17:26,399
[in unison] Yes, Madame Gazelle.

368
00:17:26,566 --> 00:17:30,033
Madame Gazelle used to teach
all the mommies and daddies

369
00:17:30,100 --> 00:17:31,366
when they were little.

370
00:17:31,433 --> 00:17:35,633
It's quite hard, Daddy,
but you do it like this:

371
00:17:36,433 --> 00:17:39,200
Let me see if I've got that right.

372
00:17:42,133 --> 00:17:45,000
Daddy, you can play the drums.

373
00:17:45,066 --> 00:17:48,300
I am a bit of an expert at drumming.

374
00:17:51,100 --> 00:17:53,466
That's good shake, rattle, and banging.

375
00:17:53,533 --> 00:17:55,033
Now for a tune.

376
00:18:13,066 --> 00:18:17,200
My daddy can shake, rattle, and bang.

377
00:18:17,266 --> 00:18:18,766
[laughing]

